{"call_id":"7a4a4c42-b7bd-43e2-86ce-2d6ecd9290f0","metadata":{"error_type":null,"finish_reason":"stop","mode":"ok","response_id":"e9239753a53dab9b4ea7348e88f0df73.9ce1d2122adce34b6da749f63c2d8d4e","status_code":null,"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cached_tokens":10496,"completion_tokens":8043,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"prompt_tokens":17223,"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cache_write_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":10496,"image_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"total_tokens":25266}},"raw_response":{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null,"message":{"annotations":null,"audio":null,"content":"{\n  \"protocol_version\": \"impact-response-v5\",\n  \"action\": \"finish\",\n  \"unit_outcome\": \"analyzed\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"case_refs\": [],\n    \"difference_refs\": [],\n    \"ranges\": [],\n    \"segment_refs\": []\n  },\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R1\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"该规则属于订单保留期调整；当前用例目标、步骤与预期均针对未登录管理访问拒绝，且执行说明要求通读全部步骤并保留负向条件，固定内容中无保留期、过期查询或相关拒绝预期，因此对该用例无影响。\",\n          \"citations\": [\n            \"F6\",\n            \"F22\",\n            \"F23\",\n            \"F24\",\n            \"F25\",\n            \"F26\",\n            \"F27\"\n          ],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R2\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"该规则删除优惠码相关需求；当前用例无优惠码提交、订单金额扣减或优惠结果校验，固定 JSON 与执行说明中也不存在对应待验证点，因此对该用例无影响。\",\n          \"citations\": [\n            \"F6\",\n            \"F22\",\n            \"F23\",\n            \"F24\",\n            \"F25\",\n            \"F26\",\n            \"F27\"\n          ],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R3\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"该规则新增订单导出能力；当前用例无导出请求、排序条件或导出结果预期，因此对该用例无影响。新增规则所需的独立覆盖范围不属于当前用例影响结论。\",\n          \"citations\": [\n            \"F6\",\n            \"F22\",\n            \"F23\",\n            \"F24\",\n            \"F25\",\n            \"F26\",\n            \"F27\"\n          ],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_outcomes\": [],\n  \"unresolved\": [],\n  \"summary\": \"用例阶段已核对 C2 固定完整 JSON、执行说明、编写来源及 R1-R3 规则证据。三条规则对 C2 均为无影响：规则变更分别涉及订单保留期调整、优惠码需求删除、订单导出新增，均未出现在该未登录管理访问拒绝用例的目标、步骤或预期中；刻意负向条件已保留。部署状态未知，所有结论待评审；未执行测试或修改正式记录。\"\n}","function_call":null,"reasoning":"The user wants me to produce a single `impact-response-v5` JSON object based on the provided input. Let me carefully analyze the context.\n\nKey facts from the input:\n1. `coordination_context.stage` is `\"case_impacts\"`. This means we are in the case stage, not discovery.\n2. `primary_ref` is `\"C2\"`.\n3. Rules available: R1, R2, R3 corresponding to:\n   - R1: `order_retention_period_days` (modified: 7 days -> 9 days)\n   - R2: `promotion_code_promo5` (removed)\n   - R3: `order_export_endpoint` (added)\n4. The primary case C2 is version `7b4d92fc-e4b8-408f-b24b-9a18077d41be`.\n5. Fixed case evidence F1-F27 all reference C2. Values are said to already be in complete reads. We must not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes in citations? Wait: \"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them.\" So in the response JSON, citations should just be [\"F1\"], etc. Reasons can mention content, but not output paths as citations? Actually it says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Probably means don't include the path strings like \"steps[0].action\" or values. But we can describe them in reason text? \"preserve deliberate negative conditions.\" Let's be careful: The schema citations are strings like `^F[1-9][0-9]*$`. So only F refs.\n\n6. Current stage protocol: `case_instruction`: \"对每条rules读取当前完整固定JSON、自身说明及已提供的编写来源。逐R引用返回当前用例影响与真实字段值；保留负向条件。discovery_results保留未完成范围，发现没有合法规则不能据此宣称无变化；没有规则也核对来源是否充分，缺少时保持依据不足。所有候选待评审，部署未知；evidence_outcomes为空，不重新提交文档发现。\"\n\n7. `analysis_protocol.instruction`: \"Return one impact-response-v5 JSON object. Follow the current coordination stage. For finish, unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null, and reads empty. Discovery: ... Case stage: assess every R rule for the current complete case identified by primary_ref, using its entire JSON, execution_notes, original sources and rule evidence. Return rule_ref/case_impacts for that current case; evidence_outcomes is empty. Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage. Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Case metadata titles are not content_json fields. The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them. For read request only needed fixed P/S/C/D reads with no candidates, evidence_outcomes or outcome. Other catalogs are retrieval metadata, not supplied evidence. Preserve deliberate negative conditions. unresolved contains only specific missing evidence that prevents CURRENT stage judgments, naming affected rules or members; use evidence_insufficient/uncertain where that evidence is needed. When the current analysis is complete, unresolved is empty. Do not put deployment unknown, pending review, preserved negative conditions, unchanged rules or separately assigned later tasks there just to restate their status. Keep those statements in summary, reasons and rule uncertainties. Existing source warnings remain explicit; never hide a gap affecting a judgment. All proposals pending review, deployment unknown. Do not execute tests or change official records.\"\n\n8. We need to assess every R rule for C2. R1, R2, R3.\n\nCase C2 content:\n- case_key: \"unauth\"\n- title: \"验证未登录拒绝管理访问\"\n- objective: \"验证未登录拒绝管理访问\" (F6)\n- extension: {\"false\":false, \"null\":null, \"zero\":0} (F2-F5)\n- steps:\n  - steps 0-6: action \"记录受控环境信息1\" ... \"记录受控环境信息7\" (F8-F23)\n  - step 7: action \"保持未登录，请求GET /admin\" (F24? Actually F24 is steps[7]. Wait let's map:\n    F24: path [\"steps\",7]\n    F25: path [\"steps\",7,\"action\"] - value \"保持未登录，请求GET /admin\"\n    F26: path [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"] - value 401\n    F27: path [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"] - value false? Wait F27 in fixed_case_evidence: {\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}. Let me re-read:\n    F25: [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]\n    F26: [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]\n    F27: root execution_notes path [].\n    Actually the JSON for fixed_case_evidence:\n    \"F25\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n    \"F26\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n    \"F27\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n    The complete case shows:\n    \"steps\": [..., {\"action\":\"保持未登录，请求GET /admin\",\"expected\":{\"login\":false,\"status\":401}}]\n    So F25 value is false, F26 value is 401, F24 is the whole step object.\n    execution_notes: \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\" (F27)\n\nOriginal source of C2: The case has `source_refs` pointing to old document parse snapshot `57e86e2c...` (requirements-v1.md, old version eb47261b). Source links also show evidence_id for old document parse snapshot. So the case was authored against the OLD document version. Important for impact assessment.\n\nNow rules:\n- R1: order retention changed 7->9 days. Does C2 impact it? C2 tests unauthenticated admin access. It has no steps related to order retention, order days, querying expired orders, 410. So no impact. Level none.\n  Citations: Need to cite case fields proving scope? The instruction says \"逐R引用返回当前用例影响与真实字段值\". For no impact, we still need citations? Schema `CaseAnchoredCandidate` requires citations minItems 1, even for level none. It says \"case_impacts minItems 1\" for each rule assessment. So for each rule we must include at least one case_impact object, even if level none. It must include citations. So for R1 none, cite objective/step fields that define scope? We can cite F6 objective and F24/F25/F26 step7? But R1 unrelated. We need to justify no impact by citing content that defines the case is about admin auth, not retention. Use F6 (objective) and maybe F24/F25 (step7 action). That should suffice.\n  Reason: 当前用例目标与步骤均围绕未登录访问 GET /admin 返回 401/False，无订单保留期、410 或保留天数相关操作、条件与预期，故不受 R1 影响。\n  Keep negative conditions: The case includes extension false/null/zero and 7 dummy steps. But not relevant to R1. For R2/R3 similarly.\n\n- R2: promotion_code_promo5 removed. C2 has no promo code. No impact.\n  Reason: 用例未涉及优惠码 PROMO5、订单金额扣减或提交优惠码操作，无相关预期，故不受 R2 影响。\n  Citations: F6, F24/F25 maybe.\n\n- R3: order_export_endpoint added (GET /orders/export). C2 has no order export. No impact.\n  Reason: 用例未涉及订单导出接口、导出排序或创建时间条件，无相关预期，故不受 R3 影响。\n  Citations: F6, F24/F25 maybe.\n\nNeed include `execution_notes` citation? For negative conditions: \"保留刻意缺失的负向条件\" and \"extension false/null/zero\" are deliberate. But for each rule no impact, not necessary? Maybe cite F27 execution_notes to show reviewed all steps and preserved negative conditions? Better to include F27 in at least the reasons? But citations field is for case impact. We can include F27 in citations for all rule assessments? It says case citations are F strings for stated case_ref. F27 is execution_notes. It supports that all steps were read and negative conditions preserved. However citing F27 for every rule might be weird, but valid. Should we cite F27 to demonstrate full read? The instructions: \"using its entire JSON, execution_notes, original sources and rule evidence.\" We should probably cite F27 in at least R1/R2/R3 or summary. But citations are per case impact. Could include F27 in each case impact to show execution_notes read and negative conditions preserved. Yet F27 doesn't prove absence of promo/export. It proves method. The impact judgment should cite content fields that show scope. For no impact, citing objective and final auth step is enough.\n\nNeed `unresolved`: Empty when analysis complete. Are there missing evidence preventing current judgments? No. The old source is provided and complete. Deployment unknown is not unresolved. So unresolved = [].\n\nNeed `unit_outcome`: \"analyzed\" for finish. reads empty (maybe need reads field? The schema has reads optional. For finish, reads empty. We can omit `reads` or include empty? The instruction: \"For finish, unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null, and reads empty.\" The schema requires action finish maybe with reads empty. Since JSON object properties include reads; not required. But to be safe maybe include `\"reads\": {\"case_refs\":[],\"difference_refs\":[],\"ranges\":[],\"segment_refs\":[]}` or omit? The schema `BoundReadRequest` has all optional arrays? It doesn't specify required. But \"reads empty\" likely means no read requests. Omit reads is fine, but schema has `reads` property optional. To be safe, include empty reads object? The instruction says \"reads empty\" not \"no reads key\". Many such protocol responses omit reads. But `action: finish` with `unit_outcome` and no candidates? We do have candidates. `evidence_outcomes` empty for case stage. Could omit evidence_outcomes? Schema optional. Might include empty array? The instruction: \"evidence_outcomes is empty.\" We can set `\"evidence_outcomes\": []` to be explicit. Also `action`: \"finish\".\n\nNeed `summary`: Must be min length 1. Should state case C2 assessment complete: reviewed fixed JSON, execution_notes, original source (old doc) and rules R1-R3; no impact for all three; deployment unknown; all proposals pending review? Wait in case stage we are returning assessments, not proposals? We return candidates of type `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment` (with rule_ref and case_impacts). No document_citations required. We should not include rule change proposals again. `candidates` items can be either `CaseAnchoredRuleCandidate` or `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment`. We should output assessments for R1, R2, R3. Action finish because we don't need additional reads.\n  Summary should mention rule outcomes and pending review/deployment unknown. It can state no execution or record changes.\n\nNeed each candidate:\n- {\n    \"rule_ref\": \"R1\",\n    \"case_impacts\": [\n      {\n        \"case_ref\":\"C2\",\n        \"level\":\"none\",\n        \"reason\":\"用例目标与全部步骤均针对未登录访问 GET /admin 的 401/false 负向校验，固定 JSON、执行说明及编写来源中无订单保留期、410 或 7/9 天相关操作、条件或预期，因此 R1 不影响当前用例。\",\n        \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n        \"verification_points\": []\n      }\n    ]\n  }\nBut `verification_points` optional? Schema `CaseAnchoredCandidate` properties includes verification_points, not required. Required: case_ref, level, reason, citations. So can omit verification_points or include [].\nFor level none, verification_points might be irrelevant; maybe include [] to be safe. But minItems? No minItems for verification_points. Include empty array.\n\nFor R2 similar citations maybe F6,F24,F25,F26,F27.\nFor R3 similar.\n\nNeed ensure citations valid F refs for C2. F1-F27 all valid. We can use F6/F24/F25/F26/F27. Maybe also F2-F5 extension? For extension negative conditions? Let's examine C2 extension: {\"false\":false,\"null\":null,\"zero\":0}. These are deliberate negative conditions? Maybe not relevant. Execution notes says keep deliberate missing negative conditions. The step7 expected only has login false and status 401. There is no other expected missing fields? Maybe extension is a distractor. We shouldn't invent. We can mention in summary: preserved deliberate negative conditions (extension false/null/zero and execution_notes) remain in place. But unresolved empty.\n\nPotential issue: Since primary case source_refs old document version includes \"管理鉴权\" section. The case tests admin auth. There is a rule in old doc for admin auth, but there is NO rule R for admin auth (unchanged). The discovery results only include changed rules: retention, promo removal, export added. The unchanged admin auth rule is not in R list. The instruction says \"assess every R rule\" not unchanged doc rules. So only R1-R3. We should not create an unchanged rule assessment. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Case metadata titles are not content_json fields.\" We should not cite title (not in F evidence anyway). Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"All proposals pending review, deployment unknown.\" In case stage, our candidates are assessments, not proposals, but should note in summary. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null\" only for finish. We choose analyzed.\n\nPotential issue: \"Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage.\" We have fixed_case_catalog includes C1 and C3 but we have no evidence values for them. We should not assess them. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"No read request\" because all fixed evidence supplied. The `additional_fixed_reads` includes some document segments, but case evidence values are in complete reads. We don't need reads. Action finish.\n\nNeed ensure JSON strictly matches schema. Let's draft:\n\n{\n  \"protocol_version\": \"impact-response-v5\",\n  \"action\": \"finish\",\n  \"unit_outcome\": \"analyzed\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"case_refs\": [],\n    \"difference_refs\": [],\n    \"ranges\": [],\n    \"segment_refs\": []\n  },\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R1\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"当前固定用例内容与执行说明均只覆盖未登录访问 GET /admin 的 401/false 负向校验，未出现订单保留期、超过保留期查询或 410 预期，也无 7/9 天保留时长相关操作或条件，因此 R1 不影响该用例。\",\n          \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R2\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"用例全部步骤和预期围绕未登录管理访问拒绝，未提交优惠码，无订单金额扣减或 PROMO5 条件，固定 JSON 与执行说明也未保留相关待验证点，因此 R2 不影响该用例。\",\n          \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R3\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"用例未涉及 GET /orders/export、订单导出或创建时间倒序排列，无相关操作、条件或预期；固定 JSON、执行说明及编写来源中也不存在导出验证点，因此 R3 不影响该用例。\",\n          \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_outcomes\": [],\n  \"unresolved\": [],\n  \"summary\": \"用例阶段已完成 C2 固定完整 JSON、执行说明、旧版编写来源与 R1-R3 规则证据的核对。三条规则对该用例均无影响：R1 保留期 7→9、R2 删除 PROMO5、R3 新增订单导出，都未出现在 C2 的未登录管理访问目标、步骤或 401/false 预期中；刻意负向条件已保留。部署状态未知，全部结论待评审；未执行测试或修改正式记录。\"\n}\n\nNeed consider if including `verification_points` empty is okay. It is property but optional. Fine.\nNeed consider if `reads` object should be empty or omitted. The schema BoundReadRequest properties are arrays, not required. If include empty arrays, valid. \"reads empty\" satisfied.\nNeed consider if `evidence_outcomes` should be omitted instead of empty. Both valid? The schema property evidence_outcomes optional with max 100. Empty array is okay. The instruction says empty. Good.\nNeed consider if citations F24/F25/F26/F27 are appropriate for every rule. F24 is path steps[7] (whole step object), F25 steps[7].expected.login, F26 steps[7].expected.status. Actually F24 in the fixed_case_evidence map is path [\"steps\",7], not [\"steps\",7,\"expected\"]. Let's verify: \n\"F22\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",6]},\n\"F23\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",6,\"action\"]},\n\"F24\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7]},\n\"F25\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"action\"]},\n\"F26\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]},\n\"F27\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]}\nWait I misread earlier! Let's re-read carefully. The input fixed_case_evidence:\n```\n\"F1\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F10\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",1],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F11\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",1,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F12\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",2],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F13\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",2,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F14\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",3],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F15\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",3,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F16\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",4],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F17\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",4,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F18\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",5],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F19\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",5,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F2\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"extension\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F20\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F21\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F22\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F23\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F24\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F25\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F26\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F27\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n```\nActually yes from input:\n```\n\"F22\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7]},\n\"F23\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"action\"]},\n\"F24\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"expected\"]},\n\"F25\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]},\n\"F26\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]},\n\"F27\": {\"path\": [], \"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n```\nLet's look exactly at user JSON:\n```\n\"F20\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6]...\n\"F21\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6,\"action\"]...\n\"F22\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7]...\n\"F23\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"action\"]...\n\"F24\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\"]...\n\"F25\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]...\n\"F26\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]...\n\"F27\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n```\nYes correct mapping:\n- F22: whole steps[7]\n- F23: steps[7].action = 保持未登录，请求GET /admin\n- F24: steps[7].expected = {\"login\":false,\"status\":401}\n- F25: steps[7].expected.login = false\n- F26: steps[7].expected.status = 401\n- F27: execution_notes = \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\"\n\nSo citations should be F6 (objective), F22, F23, F24, F25, F26, F27. Not F24/F25/F26 as action. Good catch. Need use correct refs. We should not output paths/values/hashes, but reasons can mention expected? \"401/false\" is values? It says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Wait \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\" This may apply to case citations? It says \"Case citations are F strings... Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. The server binds T/F selections...\" It might prohibit outputting the literal path or value inside citations? Since citations are just F strings. But reasons also should avoid values? It says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. This could be strict: in the JSON response, don't include field paths or values; let server bind them. However the earlier `analysis_protocol` says \"Return rule_ref/case_impacts ... using its entire JSON\". The reasons often need describe content. But it explicitly says \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\" To be safe, we should avoid exact values and paths in reasons. But the user also said \"produce review candidates\" and skill says \"用例依据引用固定版本、内容哈希和真实 JSON 路径，不用当前版本替代.\" There's tension. The protocol instruction explicitly forbids outputting paths/values in case citations? Let's parse exact wording:\n\n\"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Case metadata titles are not content_json fields. The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them.\"\n\nThus we should not include literal field paths like \"steps[7].expected.status\" or values like 401, false in the output. But can we mention high-level content like \"未登录管理访问拒绝\" without exact path/value? Yes. Need avoid exact numeric values? Maybe 401 is a value from document/case; avoid if strict. Use \"管理访问拒绝预期\" instead of 401/false. Similarly avoid \"7→9\" in reasons? Those are rule document values already in discovery. But output values maybe prohibited? The clause specifically under case citations, but likely applies to F selections. It says don't output paths/values/UUIDs/hashes. The server binds T/F. In document discovery candidates reason previously included values. But here for case stage, be cautious.\n\nNeed also not output UUIDs/hashes. We won't.\nNeed not output paths. We won't.\nNeed not output values? There is risk if summary mentions 7→9, PROMO5, GET /orders/export (document values). Are those \"values\"? They are document values from T evidence, not case F? The instruction might mean don't output the resolved path/value for F citations in textual fields. But to be safe, avoid exact values maybe. However skill requires communicate reasons clearly and preserve negative conditions. It is okay to mention rule summaries but not paths/hashes. The final output can mention \"保留期调整\" instead of \"7→9\", \"优惠码规则删除\" instead of \"PROMO5\", \"订单导出新增\" instead of \"GET /orders/export\"? But maybe too vague. The protocol for case stage says \"逐R引用返回当前用例影响与真实字段值\" then \"Do not output paths, values...\" This is contradictory: \"真实字段值\" vs \"values are already in complete reads. Do not output paths, values.\" It means select F strings, not manually output values. The server binds values. So we should use citations only to represent values. Reasons can summarize qualitative impact but avoid reprinting exact case field values? I'd avoid exact path/value. Mentioning rule keys may be okay because they are not fixed evidence values? Rule keys are provided. But again output maybe okay.\n\nNeed decide if reasons can mention \"R1 保留期调整\". It doesn't output document value numbers. Good.\n\nNeed ensure preserving deliberate negative conditions: We can mention in summary \"刻意缺失的负向条件已保留，未据此推断规则变化。\" No exact values.\n\nPotential issue: For no impact candidate, `level` enum options are none, minor, major, uncertain. We choose none.\nPotential issue: For each rule assessment, `case_impacts` minItems 1. We provide one for C2. Good.\nPotential issue: `candidates` schema allows anyOf; our objects are `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment`. Good.\nPotential issue: `applicability_suggestion` is only for rule candidate. We don't use. Good.\nPotential issue: \"discovery_results保留未完成范围\" means discovery results stay as prior, not re-evaluate. We ignore.\nPotential issue: \"发现没有合法规则不能据此宣称无变化；没有规则也核对来源是否充分，缺少时保持依据不足。\" Here rules exist. Good.\nPotential issue: environment deployment unknown. Not unresolved. Good in summary.\nPotential issue: source gaps empty. Good.\nPotential issue: no additional reads. Good.\nPotential issue: original source old doc: case source_refs only old document, not new. The rule changes are from old to new. Case was authored against old doc. For R1 retention modification: the case doesn't test retention. Thus no impact despite old source. For R2 promo removed: case doesn't use promo. For R3 export added: no export. Could the addition of order export require new coverage? But for this specific case, no impact. The protocol says assess each rule for current complete case, not identify missing project coverage. New coverage might be separate task, not case impact. \"新增规则\" might affect case? Only if case touches related operation. It does not. Good.\n\nNeed maybe for R3 added, some might say \"new rule may require new case; but current case unaffected.\" We can state no impact for C2, and note new coverage remains outside current case impact (but not unresolved). Good in reason or summary.\nPotential issue: Do not say \"准备成功\" or \"测试通过\". We won't.\n\nLet's craft final JSON with careful reasons not including paths/values/hashes. The summary may mention no impact and pending review.\n\nNeed perhaps `unit_outcome` can be \"analyzed\" even though all impacts none. Yes.\nNeed perhaps `unresolved` empty. But one might argue deployment unknown prevents applicability decisions (current/future), but protocol says deployment unknown is not unresolved; keep in summary/reasons. Good.\n\nLet's ensure final output is only JSON object, no markdown? User requested \"Return one impact-response-v5 JSON object.\" We should output raw JSON only. No code fences? Usually final answer should be JSON. We'll output plain JSON.\n\nNeed check JSON valid:\n- All required top-level: protocol_version, action, summary. We have.\n- unit_outcome required non-null for finish. We have.\n- reads empty arrays.\n- candidates:\n  - top-level candidate CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment requires rule_ref and case_impacts. We have.\n  - case_impacts item requires case_ref, level, reason, citations. We have.\n  - verification_points optional but include empty array.\n- evidence_outcomes empty.\n- unresolved empty.\n\nCitations: For R1/R2/R3 no impact:\n  F6 objective, F22 step7, F23 action, F24 expected, F25 expected login, F26 expected status, F27 execution notes. All valid. Maybe too many but okay. Could use F6,F22,F23,F24,F27. F25/F26 are exact nested fields but valid. Use all to show full step expected. We should not include F1 (whole content_json) maybe okay. But F1 is content_json root. Not needed. If we include F1, that's fine. But citations minItems 1. Good.\n  The rule evidence T refs? In case stage, `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment` has no document_citations. The rule_ref identifies rule. Case citations only F. We don't need T. The `rule_ref` maps to rule with T evidence. Good.\n\nNeed reason texts avoid case values. But they can mention objective/step nature:\n- \"当前用例目标与末步均针对未登录管理访问拒绝，执行说明要求通读全部步骤并保留负向条件；固定内容中无该规则涉及业务操作、条件或预期。\" Good.\n\nFor R1: \"该规则属于订单保留期调整；当前用例既无保留期相关请求，也无过期查询或拒绝保留访问的预期，故无影响。\"\nFor R2: \"该规则删除优惠码相关需求；当前用例无优惠码提交或金额扣减步骤与预期，故无影响。\"\nFor R3: \"该规则新增订单导出能力；当前用例无导出请求、排序或导出结果校验，故无影响；新增规则是否形成独立覆盖不属于当前用例影响。\"\n\nThese mention \"订单保留期\", \"优惠码\", \"订单导出\" - these are rule concepts, not exact values. Should be fine. Could mention \"PROMO5\"? Avoid exact code. \"GET /orders/export\" is API path, maybe a value; avoid. Reason says export endpoint? \"导出接口\" enough. Avoid \"GET\". Good.\n\nSummary:\n\"用例阶段已核对 C2 固定完整 JSON、执行说明、旧编写来源及 R1-R3 规则证据。R1-R3 对 C2 均为无影响：规则变更分别涉及订单保留期调整、优惠码需求删除、订单导出新增，均未出现在该未登录管理访问拒绝用例的目标、步骤或预期中；执行说明中的刻意负向条件已保留。部署状态未知，所有结论待评审；未执行测试或修改正式记录。\"\n\nThis mentions R1-R3 and rule concepts, no exact values/paths/hashes. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"旧编写来源\" but no UUIDs/hashes. Good.\nNeed include \"new rule may need separate coverage\" maybe: \"新增导出规则所需的独立覆盖不在本用例影响范围内。\" Could add to summary. But no need. Maybe include to avoid seeming project coverage complete. Summary can say \"新增规则的独立覆盖范围不在本用例阶段结论内。\" This is useful. It's not unresolved. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"all proposals pending review\" not proposals but assessments pending review. Good.\n\nLet's produce raw JSON.\n\nDouble-check if `reads` should be omitted. If schema action finish, reads empty. I will include empty reads object. The BoundReadRequest fields arrays; empty arrays fine. Does `additionalProperties:false` at top level allow `reads`? yes property. Good.\n\nPotential schema: `unit_outcome` anyOf with default null; for finish required non-null. We have \"analyzed\".\nPotential schema: `candidates` items anyOf; no problem.\nPotential schema: `evidence_outcomes` maxItems 100; empty okay.\nPotential schema: `unresolved` items string; empty okay.\n\nNeed ensure no trailing commas. Fine.\n\nLet's output.","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to produce a single `impact-response-v5` JSON object based on the provided input. Let me carefully analyze the context.\n\nKey facts from the input:\n1. `coordination_context.stage` is `\"case_impacts\"`. This means we are in the case stage, not discovery.\n2. `primary_ref` is `\"C2\"`.\n3. Rules available: R1, R2, R3 corresponding to:\n   - R1: `order_retention_period_days` (modified: 7 days -> 9 days)\n   - R2: `promotion_code_promo5` (removed)\n   - R3: `order_export_endpoint` (added)\n4. The primary case C2 is version `7b4d92fc-e4b8-408f-b24b-9a18077d41be`.\n5. Fixed case evidence F1-F27 all reference C2. Values are said to already be in complete reads. We must not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes in citations? Wait: \"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them.\" So in the response JSON, citations should just be [\"F1\"], etc. Reasons can mention content, but not output paths as citations? Actually it says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Probably means don't include the path strings like \"steps[0].action\" or values. But we can describe them in reason text? \"preserve deliberate negative conditions.\" Let's be careful: The schema citations are strings like `^F[1-9][0-9]*$`. So only F refs.\n\n6. Current stage protocol: `case_instruction`: \"对每条rules读取当前完整固定JSON、自身说明及已提供的编写来源。逐R引用返回当前用例影响与真实字段值；保留负向条件。discovery_results保留未完成范围，发现没有合法规则不能据此宣称无变化；没有规则也核对来源是否充分，缺少时保持依据不足。所有候选待评审，部署未知；evidence_outcomes为空，不重新提交文档发现。\"\n\n7. `analysis_protocol.instruction`: \"Return one impact-response-v5 JSON object. Follow the current coordination stage. For finish, unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null, and reads empty. Discovery: ... Case stage: assess every R rule for the current complete case identified by primary_ref, using its entire JSON, execution_notes, original sources and rule evidence. Return rule_ref/case_impacts for that current case; evidence_outcomes is empty. Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage. Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Case metadata titles are not content_json fields. The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them. For read request only needed fixed P/S/C/D reads with no candidates, evidence_outcomes or outcome. Other catalogs are retrieval metadata, not supplied evidence. Preserve deliberate negative conditions. unresolved contains only specific missing evidence that prevents CURRENT stage judgments, naming affected rules or members; use evidence_insufficient/uncertain where that evidence is needed. When the current analysis is complete, unresolved is empty. Do not put deployment unknown, pending review, preserved negative conditions, unchanged rules or separately assigned later tasks there just to restate their status. Keep those statements in summary, reasons and rule uncertainties. Existing source warnings remain explicit; never hide a gap affecting a judgment. All proposals pending review, deployment unknown. Do not execute tests or change official records.\"\n\n8. We need to assess every R rule for C2. R1, R2, R3.\n\nCase C2 content:\n- case_key: \"unauth\"\n- title: \"验证未登录拒绝管理访问\"\n- objective: \"验证未登录拒绝管理访问\" (F6)\n- extension: {\"false\":false, \"null\":null, \"zero\":0} (F2-F5)\n- steps:\n  - steps 0-6: action \"记录受控环境信息1\" ... \"记录受控环境信息7\" (F8-F23)\n  - step 7: action \"保持未登录，请求GET /admin\" (F24? Actually F24 is steps[7]. Wait let's map:\n    F24: path [\"steps\",7]\n    F25: path [\"steps\",7,\"action\"] - value \"保持未登录，请求GET /admin\"\n    F26: path [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"] - value 401\n    F27: path [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"] - value false? Wait F27 in fixed_case_evidence: {\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}. Let me re-read:\n    F25: [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]\n    F26: [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]\n    F27: root execution_notes path [].\n    Actually the JSON for fixed_case_evidence:\n    \"F25\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n    \"F26\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n    \"F27\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n    The complete case shows:\n    \"steps\": [..., {\"action\":\"保持未登录，请求GET /admin\",\"expected\":{\"login\":false,\"status\":401}}]\n    So F25 value is false, F26 value is 401, F24 is the whole step object.\n    execution_notes: \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\" (F27)\n\nOriginal source of C2: The case has `source_refs` pointing to old document parse snapshot `57e86e2c...` (requirements-v1.md, old version eb47261b). Source links also show evidence_id for old document parse snapshot. So the case was authored against the OLD document version. Important for impact assessment.\n\nNow rules:\n- R1: order retention changed 7->9 days. Does C2 impact it? C2 tests unauthenticated admin access. It has no steps related to order retention, order days, querying expired orders, 410. So no impact. Level none.\n  Citations: Need to cite case fields proving scope? The instruction says \"逐R引用返回当前用例影响与真实字段值\". For no impact, we still need citations? Schema `CaseAnchoredCandidate` requires citations minItems 1, even for level none. It says \"case_impacts minItems 1\" for each rule assessment. So for each rule we must include at least one case_impact object, even if level none. It must include citations. So for R1 none, cite objective/step fields that define scope? We can cite F6 objective and F24/F25/F26 step7? But R1 unrelated. We need to justify no impact by citing content that defines the case is about admin auth, not retention. Use F6 (objective) and maybe F24/F25 (step7 action). That should suffice.\n  Reason: 当前用例目标与步骤均围绕未登录访问 GET /admin 返回 401/False，无订单保留期、410 或保留天数相关操作、条件与预期，故不受 R1 影响。\n  Keep negative conditions: The case includes extension false/null/zero and 7 dummy steps. But not relevant to R1. For R2/R3 similarly.\n\n- R2: promotion_code_promo5 removed. C2 has no promo code. No impact.\n  Reason: 用例未涉及优惠码 PROMO5、订单金额扣减或提交优惠码操作，无相关预期，故不受 R2 影响。\n  Citations: F6, F24/F25 maybe.\n\n- R3: order_export_endpoint added (GET /orders/export). C2 has no order export. No impact.\n  Reason: 用例未涉及订单导出接口、导出排序或创建时间条件，无相关预期，故不受 R3 影响。\n  Citations: F6, F24/F25 maybe.\n\nNeed include `execution_notes` citation? For negative conditions: \"保留刻意缺失的负向条件\" and \"extension false/null/zero\" are deliberate. But for each rule no impact, not necessary? Maybe cite F27 execution_notes to show reviewed all steps and preserved negative conditions? Better to include F27 in at least the reasons? But citations field is for case impact. We can include F27 in citations for all rule assessments? It says case citations are F strings for stated case_ref. F27 is execution_notes. It supports that all steps were read and negative conditions preserved. However citing F27 for every rule might be weird, but valid. Should we cite F27 to demonstrate full read? The instructions: \"using its entire JSON, execution_notes, original sources and rule evidence.\" We should probably cite F27 in at least R1/R2/R3 or summary. But citations are per case impact. Could include F27 in each case impact to show execution_notes read and negative conditions preserved. Yet F27 doesn't prove absence of promo/export. It proves method. The impact judgment should cite content fields that show scope. For no impact, citing objective and final auth step is enough.\n\nNeed `unresolved`: Empty when analysis complete. Are there missing evidence preventing current judgments? No. The old source is provided and complete. Deployment unknown is not unresolved. So unresolved = [].\n\nNeed `unit_outcome`: \"analyzed\" for finish. reads empty (maybe need reads field? The schema has reads optional. For finish, reads empty. We can omit `reads` or include empty? The instruction: \"For finish, unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null, and reads empty.\" The schema requires action finish maybe with reads empty. Since JSON object properties include reads; not required. But to be safe maybe include `\"reads\": {\"case_refs\":[],\"difference_refs\":[],\"ranges\":[],\"segment_refs\":[]}` or omit? The schema `BoundReadRequest` has all optional arrays? It doesn't specify required. But \"reads empty\" likely means no read requests. Omit reads is fine, but schema has `reads` property optional. To be safe, include empty reads object? The instruction says \"reads empty\" not \"no reads key\". Many such protocol responses omit reads. But `action: finish` with `unit_outcome` and no candidates? We do have candidates. `evidence_outcomes` empty for case stage. Could omit evidence_outcomes? Schema optional. Might include empty array? The instruction: \"evidence_outcomes is empty.\" We can set `\"evidence_outcomes\": []` to be explicit. Also `action`: \"finish\".\n\nNeed `summary`: Must be min length 1. Should state case C2 assessment complete: reviewed fixed JSON, execution_notes, original source (old doc) and rules R1-R3; no impact for all three; deployment unknown; all proposals pending review? Wait in case stage we are returning assessments, not proposals? We return candidates of type `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment` (with rule_ref and case_impacts). No document_citations required. We should not include rule change proposals again. `candidates` items can be either `CaseAnchoredRuleCandidate` or `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment`. We should output assessments for R1, R2, R3. Action finish because we don't need additional reads.\n  Summary should mention rule outcomes and pending review/deployment unknown. It can state no execution or record changes.\n\nNeed each candidate:\n- {\n    \"rule_ref\": \"R1\",\n    \"case_impacts\": [\n      {\n        \"case_ref\":\"C2\",\n        \"level\":\"none\",\n        \"reason\":\"用例目标与全部步骤均针对未登录访问 GET /admin 的 401/false 负向校验，固定 JSON、执行说明及编写来源中无订单保留期、410 或 7/9 天相关操作、条件或预期，因此 R1 不影响当前用例。\",\n        \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n        \"verification_points\": []\n      }\n    ]\n  }\nBut `verification_points` optional? Schema `CaseAnchoredCandidate` properties includes verification_points, not required. Required: case_ref, level, reason, citations. So can omit verification_points or include [].\nFor level none, verification_points might be irrelevant; maybe include [] to be safe. But minItems? No minItems for verification_points. Include empty array.\n\nFor R2 similar citations maybe F6,F24,F25,F26,F27.\nFor R3 similar.\n\nNeed ensure citations valid F refs for C2. F1-F27 all valid. We can use F6/F24/F25/F26/F27. Maybe also F2-F5 extension? For extension negative conditions? Let's examine C2 extension: {\"false\":false,\"null\":null,\"zero\":0}. These are deliberate negative conditions? Maybe not relevant. Execution notes says keep deliberate missing negative conditions. The step7 expected only has login false and status 401. There is no other expected missing fields? Maybe extension is a distractor. We shouldn't invent. We can mention in summary: preserved deliberate negative conditions (extension false/null/zero and execution_notes) remain in place. But unresolved empty.\n\nPotential issue: Since primary case source_refs old document version includes \"管理鉴权\" section. The case tests admin auth. There is a rule in old doc for admin auth, but there is NO rule R for admin auth (unchanged). The discovery results only include changed rules: retention, promo removal, export added. The unchanged admin auth rule is not in R list. The instruction says \"assess every R rule\" not unchanged doc rules. So only R1-R3. We should not create an unchanged rule assessment. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Case metadata titles are not content_json fields.\" We should not cite title (not in F evidence anyway). Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"All proposals pending review, deployment unknown.\" In case stage, our candidates are assessments, not proposals, but should note in summary. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"unit_outcome must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null\" only for finish. We choose analyzed.\n\nPotential issue: \"Other cases may be read as supplementary evidence, but each has its own analysis task; do not turn this call into whole-project coverage.\" We have fixed_case_catalog includes C1 and C3 but we have no evidence values for them. We should not assess them. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"No read request\" because all fixed evidence supplied. The `additional_fixed_reads` includes some document segments, but case evidence values are in complete reads. We don't need reads. Action finish.\n\nNeed ensure JSON strictly matches schema. Let's draft:\n\n{\n  \"protocol_version\": \"impact-response-v5\",\n  \"action\": \"finish\",\n  \"unit_outcome\": \"analyzed\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"case_refs\": [],\n    \"difference_refs\": [],\n    \"ranges\": [],\n    \"segment_refs\": []\n  },\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R1\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"当前固定用例内容与执行说明均只覆盖未登录访问 GET /admin 的 401/false 负向校验，未出现订单保留期、超过保留期查询或 410 预期，也无 7/9 天保留时长相关操作或条件，因此 R1 不影响该用例。\",\n          \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R2\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"用例全部步骤和预期围绕未登录管理访问拒绝，未提交优惠码，无订单金额扣减或 PROMO5 条件，固定 JSON 与执行说明也未保留相关待验证点，因此 R2 不影响该用例。\",\n          \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_ref\": \"R3\",\n      \"case_impacts\": [\n        {\n          \"case_ref\": \"C2\",\n          \"level\": \"none\",\n          \"reason\": \"用例未涉及 GET /orders/export、订单导出或创建时间倒序排列，无相关操作、条件或预期；固定 JSON、执行说明及编写来源中也不存在导出验证点，因此 R3 不影响该用例。\",\n          \"citations\": [\"F6\",\"F24\",\"F25\",\"F26\",\"F27\"],\n          \"verification_points\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_outcomes\": [],\n  \"unresolved\": [],\n  \"summary\": \"用例阶段已完成 C2 固定完整 JSON、执行说明、旧版编写来源与 R1-R3 规则证据的核对。三条规则对该用例均无影响：R1 保留期 7→9、R2 删除 PROMO5、R3 新增订单导出，都未出现在 C2 的未登录管理访问目标、步骤或 401/false 预期中；刻意负向条件已保留。部署状态未知，全部结论待评审；未执行测试或修改正式记录。\"\n}\n\nNeed consider if including `verification_points` empty is okay. It is property but optional. Fine.\nNeed consider if `reads` object should be empty or omitted. The schema BoundReadRequest properties are arrays, not required. If include empty arrays, valid. \"reads empty\" satisfied.\nNeed consider if `evidence_outcomes` should be omitted instead of empty. Both valid? The schema property evidence_outcomes optional with max 100. Empty array is okay. The instruction says empty. Good.\nNeed consider if citations F24/F25/F26/F27 are appropriate for every rule. F24 is path steps[7] (whole step object), F25 steps[7].expected.login, F26 steps[7].expected.status. Actually F24 in the fixed_case_evidence map is path [\"steps\",7], not [\"steps\",7,\"expected\"]. Let's verify: \n\"F22\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",6]},\n\"F23\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",6,\"action\"]},\n\"F24\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7]},\n\"F25\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"action\"]},\n\"F26\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]},\n\"F27\":{\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]}\nWait I misread earlier! Let's re-read carefully. The input fixed_case_evidence:\n```\n\"F1\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F10\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",1],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F11\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",1,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F12\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",2],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F13\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",2,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F14\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",3],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F15\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",3,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F16\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",4],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F17\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",4,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F18\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",5],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F19\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",5,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F2\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"extension\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F20\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F21\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F22\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F23\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"action\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F24\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F25\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F26\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"],\"root\":\"content_json\"},\n\"F27\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n```\nActually yes from input:\n```\n\"F22\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7]},\n\"F23\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"action\"]},\n\"F24\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"expected\"]},\n\"F25\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]},\n\"F26\": {\"path\": [\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]},\n\"F27\": {\"path\": [], \"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n```\nLet's look exactly at user JSON:\n```\n\"F20\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6]...\n\"F21\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",6,\"action\"]...\n\"F22\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7]...\n\"F23\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"action\"]...\n\"F24\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\"]...\n\"F25\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"login\"]...\n\"F26\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[\"steps\",7,\"expected\",\"status\"]...\n\"F27\":{\"case_ref\":\"C2\",\"path\":[],\"root\":\"execution_notes\"}\n```\nYes correct mapping:\n- F22: whole steps[7]\n- F23: steps[7].action = 保持未登录，请求GET /admin\n- F24: steps[7].expected = {\"login\":false,\"status\":401}\n- F25: steps[7].expected.login = false\n- F26: steps[7].expected.status = 401\n- F27: execution_notes = \"阅读所有步骤，保留刻意缺失的负向条件。\"\n\nSo citations should be F6 (objective), F22, F23, F24, F25, F26, F27. Not F24/F25/F26 as action. Good catch. Need use correct refs. We should not output paths/values/hashes, but reasons can mention expected? \"401/false\" is values? It says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Wait \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\" This may apply to case citations? It says \"Case citations are F strings... Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. The server binds T/F selections...\" It might prohibit outputting the literal path or value inside citations? Since citations are just F strings. But reasons also should avoid values? It says do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. This could be strict: in the JSON response, don't include field paths or values; let server bind them. However the earlier `analysis_protocol` says \"Return rule_ref/case_impacts ... using its entire JSON\". The reasons often need describe content. But it explicitly says \"Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes.\" To be safe, we should avoid exact values and paths in reasons. But the user also said \"produce review candidates\" and skill says \"用例依据引用固定版本、内容哈希和真实 JSON 路径，不用当前版本替代.\" There's tension. The protocol instruction explicitly forbids outputting paths/values in case citations? Let's parse exact wording:\n\n\"Case citations are F strings from fixed_case_evidence for the stated case_ref. Each F selects a literal field path in the complete JSON or execution_notes; values are already in those complete reads. Do not output paths, values, UUIDs or hashes. Case metadata titles are not content_json fields. The server binds T/F selections to exact original positions/versions/paths/values and verifies them.\"\n\nThus we should not include literal field paths like \"steps[7].expected.status\" or values like 401, false in the output. But can we mention high-level content like \"未登录管理访问拒绝\" without exact path/value? Yes. Need avoid exact numeric values? Maybe 401 is a value from document/case; avoid if strict. Use \"管理访问拒绝预期\" instead of 401/false. Similarly avoid \"7→9\" in reasons? Those are rule document values already in discovery. But output values maybe prohibited? The clause specifically under case citations, but likely applies to F selections. It says don't output paths/values/UUIDs/hashes. The server binds T/F. In document discovery candidates reason previously included values. But here for case stage, be cautious.\n\nNeed also not output UUIDs/hashes. We won't.\nNeed not output paths. We won't.\nNeed not output values? There is risk if summary mentions 7→9, PROMO5, GET /orders/export (document values). Are those \"values\"? They are document values from T evidence, not case F? The instruction might mean don't output the resolved path/value for F citations in textual fields. But to be safe, avoid exact values maybe. However skill requires communicate reasons clearly and preserve negative conditions. It is okay to mention rule summaries but not paths/hashes. The final output can mention \"保留期调整\" instead of \"7→9\", \"优惠码规则删除\" instead of \"PROMO5\", \"订单导出新增\" instead of \"GET /orders/export\"? But maybe too vague. The protocol for case stage says \"逐R引用返回当前用例影响与真实字段值\" then \"Do not output paths, values...\" This is contradictory: \"真实字段值\" vs \"values are already in complete reads. Do not output paths, values.\" It means select F strings, not manually output values. The server binds values. So we should use citations only to represent values. Reasons can summarize qualitative impact but avoid reprinting exact case field values? I'd avoid exact path/value. Mentioning rule keys may be okay because they are not fixed evidence values? Rule keys are provided. But again output maybe okay.\n\nNeed decide if reasons can mention \"R1 保留期调整\". It doesn't output document value numbers. Good.\n\nNeed ensure preserving deliberate negative conditions: We can mention in summary \"刻意缺失的负向条件已保留，未据此推断规则变化。\" No exact values.\n\nPotential issue: For no impact candidate, `level` enum options are none, minor, major, uncertain. We choose none.\nPotential issue: For each rule assessment, `case_impacts` minItems 1. We provide one for C2. Good.\nPotential issue: `candidates` schema allows anyOf; our objects are `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment`. Good.\nPotential issue: `applicability_suggestion` is only for rule candidate. We don't use. Good.\nPotential issue: \"discovery_results保留未完成范围\" means discovery results stay as prior, not re-evaluate. We ignore.\nPotential issue: \"发现没有合法规则不能据此宣称无变化；没有规则也核对来源是否充分，缺少时保持依据不足。\" Here rules exist. Good.\nPotential issue: environment deployment unknown. Not unresolved. Good in summary.\nPotential issue: source gaps empty. Good.\nPotential issue: no additional reads. Good.\nPotential issue: original source old doc: case source_refs only old document, not new. The rule changes are from old to new. Case was authored against old doc. For R1 retention modification: the case doesn't test retention. Thus no impact despite old source. For R2 promo removed: case doesn't use promo. For R3 export added: no export. Could the addition of order export require new coverage? But for this specific case, no impact. The protocol says assess each rule for current complete case, not identify missing project coverage. New coverage might be separate task, not case impact. \"新增规则\" might affect case? Only if case touches related operation. It does not. Good.\n\nNeed maybe for R3 added, some might say \"new rule may require new case; but current case unaffected.\" We can state no impact for C2, and note new coverage remains outside current case impact (but not unresolved). Good in reason or summary.\nPotential issue: Do not say \"准备成功\" or \"测试通过\". We won't.\n\nLet's craft final JSON with careful reasons not including paths/values/hashes. The summary may mention no impact and pending review.\n\nNeed perhaps `unit_outcome` can be \"analyzed\" even though all impacts none. Yes.\nNeed perhaps `unresolved` empty. But one might argue deployment unknown prevents applicability decisions (current/future), but protocol says deployment unknown is not unresolved; keep in summary/reasons. Good.\n\nLet's ensure final output is only JSON object, no markdown? User requested \"Return one impact-response-v5 JSON object.\" We should output raw JSON only. No code fences? Usually final answer should be JSON. We'll output plain JSON.\n\nNeed check JSON valid:\n- All required top-level: protocol_version, action, summary. We have.\n- unit_outcome required non-null for finish. We have.\n- reads empty arrays.\n- candidates:\n  - top-level candidate CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment requires rule_ref and case_impacts. We have.\n  - case_impacts item requires case_ref, level, reason, citations. We have.\n  - verification_points optional but include empty array.\n- evidence_outcomes empty.\n- unresolved empty.\n\nCitations: For R1/R2/R3 no impact:\n  F6 objective, F22 step7, F23 action, F24 expected, F25 expected login, F26 expected status, F27 execution notes. All valid. Maybe too many but okay. Could use F6,F22,F23,F24,F27. F25/F26 are exact nested fields but valid. Use all to show full step expected. We should not include F1 (whole content_json) maybe okay. But F1 is content_json root. Not needed. If we include F1, that's fine. But citations minItems 1. Good.\n  The rule evidence T refs? In case stage, `CaseAnchoredRuleAssessment` has no document_citations. The rule_ref identifies rule. Case citations only F. We don't need T. The `rule_ref` maps to rule with T evidence. Good.\n\nNeed reason texts avoid case values. But they can mention objective/step nature:\n- \"当前用例目标与末步均针对未登录管理访问拒绝，执行说明要求通读全部步骤并保留负向条件；固定内容中无该规则涉及业务操作、条件或预期。\" Good.\n\nFor R1: \"该规则属于订单保留期调整；当前用例既无保留期相关请求，也无过期查询或拒绝保留访问的预期，故无影响。\"\nFor R2: \"该规则删除优惠码相关需求；当前用例无优惠码提交或金额扣减步骤与预期，故无影响。\"\nFor R3: \"该规则新增订单导出能力；当前用例无导出请求、排序或导出结果校验，故无影响；新增规则是否形成独立覆盖不属于当前用例影响。\"\n\nThese mention \"订单保留期\", \"优惠码\", \"订单导出\" - these are rule concepts, not exact values. Should be fine. Could mention \"PROMO5\"? Avoid exact code. \"GET /orders/export\" is API path, maybe a value; avoid. Reason says export endpoint? \"导出接口\" enough. Avoid \"GET\". Good.\n\nSummary:\n\"用例阶段已核对 C2 固定完整 JSON、执行说明、旧编写来源及 R1-R3 规则证据。R1-R3 对 C2 均为无影响：规则变更分别涉及订单保留期调整、优惠码需求删除、订单导出新增，均未出现在该未登录管理访问拒绝用例的目标、步骤或预期中；执行说明中的刻意负向条件已保留。部署状态未知，所有结论待评审；未执行测试或修改正式记录。\"\n\nThis mentions R1-R3 and rule concepts, no exact values/paths/hashes. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"旧编写来源\" but no UUIDs/hashes. Good.\nNeed include \"new rule may need separate coverage\" maybe: \"新增导出规则所需的独立覆盖不在本用例影响范围内。\" Could add to summary. But no need. Maybe include to avoid seeming project coverage complete. Summary can say \"新增规则的独立覆盖范围不在本用例阶段结论内。\" This is useful. It's not unresolved. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"all proposals pending review\" not proposals but assessments pending review. Good.\n\nLet's produce raw JSON.\n\nDouble-check if `reads` should be omitted. If schema action finish, reads empty. I will include empty reads object. The BoundReadRequest fields arrays; empty arrays fine. Does `additionalPr